# File store and documents

This run has a file store in the file system, outside the working directory. Its absolute path is
in the environment variable `RAGENTS_FILES_DIR` (in bash: `echo $RAGENTS_FILES_DIR`).

- Create one subdirectory per topic: `$RAGENTS_FILES_DIR/<topic>/`.
- Put documents, reports and temporary products there - NOT into the working directory, unless
  they are part of the actual assignment.
- The user sees these files in the "Dokumente" area of the interface, grouped by subdirectory.
- When you spawn agents, name in their assignment the store path they are supposed to write to.

If the user wants to see the content of a file or a document, show it COMPLETELY via
`show_document` (title = file name or document name) - never paraphrase or shorten. Files of the
file store you show via `path`, relative to the store. Everything else - files from your working
directory and content you produced yourself - you pass via `content`; `path` finds nothing outside
the file store.
